===Japan vs Poland===
The two teams had met twice, most recently in a friendly game in 2002, won by Japan 2–0.<ref name=Kit16/>

[[Yoshinori Muto]]'s drive forced [[Łukasz Fabiański]] to parry, before the goalkeeper smothered a [[Gōtoku Sakai]] effort. [[Eiji Kawashima]] scooped [[Kamil Grosicki]]'s header clear. With just over half an hour remaining, [[Rafał Kurzawa]]'s free-kick from the left picked out [[Jan Bednarek]], who volleyed it into the net from six yards out. [[Maya Yoshida]] headed well wide from a left-wing corner. [[Robert Lewandowski]] steered Grosicki's pin-point pass over the top.<ref name="JPN-POL recap">{{cite web |url=https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/jpn-pol-review-364-words-2972833 |title=Japan progress despite defeat |publisher=FIFA |date=28 June 2018 |access-date=28 June 2018 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260520052747/https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/jpn-pol-review-364-words-2972833 |archive-date=20 May 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Spratt |first=Ben |title=Fair play history made as Nishino's men scrape through |url=http://www.goal.com/en/news/8/main/2018/06/28/45933682/japan-0-poland-1-fair-play-history-made-as-nishinos-men |website=Goal.com |date=28 June 2018}}</ref>

Poland beat Japan for the first time in an official match, having defeated Japan in four unofficial matches. Poland won each of their 14 games in which they scored first in World Cup finals. Poland  kept a clean sheet at the World Cup for the first time since winning [[1986 FIFA World Cup Group F#Poland vs Portugal|1–0]] against Portugal in 1986.<ref>{{cite web |last=Hafez |first=Shamoon |title=Japan 0 Poland 1 |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/44439298 |work=BBC Sport |date=28 June 2018}}</ref> On another side, since the new millennium, Poland had repeated their poor performances in 2002 and 2006 World Cups, eliminated after losing two opening matches before grabbing a late victory in the final match.

There was some criticism of the final minutes in the game, as both sides appeared to settle for the 1–0 scoreline.<ref>[https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/44649668 Japan go through but final group game ends in 'mind-boggling farce']</ref>

